      "writtenOn": "2023-01-03T23:20:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, after looking this over some more I realized:\n1. The _device_ doesn\u0027t have to support RKP for the customer, but the HAL needs to work -- this is the CDD requirement (though, philosophically, it\u0027s a strange requirement).\n2. These tests are only verifying the integration of the KeyMint HAL and the IRPC HAL. For example, if a device shipped on Android 13 (with KeyMint 2) and a VSR-11 chipset, then we should skip this test.\n\n\u003e IIRC, Keymint 2 was shipped with Android 12\nLooks like it\u0027s Android 13, actually. (VSR links are internal only, not sharing here). However, the `Vsr13Test` seems to confirm this.\n\nThese version checks are somehow more confusing then it seems the should be on the surface.",
